WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:05.000
This concludes the material that will 
be covered on the final exam...

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.810
I wish you all the best of luck.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.430
What're you doing, Ayase?

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.980
That's not gonna be on the test.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.400
You've been top of your game 
in karuta since that last win.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.680
Mashima should be the only one
feeling all gloomy.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.450
I think losing to Wataya Arata and getting
fourth prize is pretty darn good, myself...

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.090
<i>Taichi...</i>

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.210
<i>In the sleepy...</i>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.590
<i>Said bed was cold...</i>

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.380
<i>It looks like he's just... playing karuta.</i>

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.180
<i>Taichi...</i>

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.210
<i>Why did you enter
the Takamatsu Memorial Cup alone?</i>

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.480
<i>What happened in your match with Arata?</i>

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.290
<i>I'm so close to you all the time,</i>

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.470
<i>so why can't I ask you 
these things anymore?</i>

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.070
<b>Do Not Open! 
Girls Changing Inside 
Don't you dare!! Don't!</b>

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.400
Chihaya-chan, Hanano-san...

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.740
Don't you feel like we need to do 
something about the mood around here?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.600
Finals are coming up, the summer 
tournament's still far off,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.280
and the president's feeling down.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.400
We should do something.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.030
L-Like what?

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.140
And how?

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.730
I-It needs to be something fun.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.360
February...

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.250
is when Valentine's Day is!

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.850
We girls should all make chocolates

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.340
to bring this club's vitality back!

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:39.150
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.980
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.970
Verse 22

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.970
Just 
as my 
beauty 
has 
faded

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.030
Something smells good!

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:48.490
What're you up to, Chihaya?

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.040
Don't come in here, Dad!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.560
O-Okay... Good luck, then.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.190
<b>Chocolate Recipes Starting with the 
Most Delicious Bases</b>

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.200
"Enrobe the balls of ganache."

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.100
Enrobe them? Like this?

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.330
Roll the ganache into 
balls in your hands...

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.070
Enrobe...

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.070
It started out this big

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.070
<b>Melted Off</b>

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.670
Roll...

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:06.830
<b>Dissolved
 to Nothing</b>

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.040
What now?!

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.560
We're gonna run out of ingredients 
before Sumire-chan gets here!

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.640
Hanano-san did say she'd 
be about an hour late!

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.000
I'll go buy chocolate bars 
from the convenience store!

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.260
What are you two doing?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.170
I told you not to start before I got here!

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.780
I've been making chocolates 
since I was in second grade.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.350
I make tons of it to give 
my friends every year,

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.390
so I have plenty of wrapping 
and other tools, too.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.520
You can ask me anything.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.280
<b>Such a girl!!</b>

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.280
All I can cook is rice...

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.940
In fact, I'd venture to say that 
chocolate-making for beginners

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.400
is all about making something far removed
from chocolate and <i>presenting</i> it as chocolate.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.490
What does that mean?

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.040
If a beginner just melts chocolate bars
and reforms them into different shapes,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.410
you can't temper it, so it'll just 
separate and drop in quality.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:58.130
<b>Te... 
Temper
...?</b>

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.500
If you stick close to the original chocolate,

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.140
it'll never match up to the 
stuff you can buy in stores.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:01.930
In my experience, the best chocolates 
that leave the best impression

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.150
are the ones made with flour and cocoa!

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.530
Flour and cocoa?

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:06.510
Not chocolate?

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.080
Today we'll be making chocolate waffles,
 cocoa marshmallows,

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.240
and black cocoa shortbread cookies.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.650
They're filling, perfect for boys, 
and don't need refrigeration.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:22.500
<i>Wow... Hanano-san really does 
calculate everything in life!</i>

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.710
Ayase-senpai!

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.650
Proportions are everything in baking,
so measure properly!

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:30.650
<i>I didn't know sweets and Valentines 
could make someone shine so bright!</i>

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.660
Oe-senpai, you need
 to measure, too!

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.120
Let's start the Valentine's cooking!

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:33.410
<b>Valentine's Cooking!!</b>

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.710
Knead the dough well to produce plenty of gluten

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.710
Add the butter in three 
separate portions and
 knead well to make it shine

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:46.800
<b>Chocolate Waffles</b>

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.710
<b>Let the dough rise to
 1.5x the original size</b>

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.250
<b>Add chocolate 
chips and fold</b>

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.010
After proofing, cook on low heat

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.920
<b>3-4 minutes on both sides</b>

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.710
W-W...

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.800
Wow!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.890
It's so good!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.060
Smells
 great!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.050
No eating! We're moving on!

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.060
Mix corn syrup, sugar, 
cocoa, and water in a
small pan, warm to 125°C,
 then add gelatin

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.060
Break up egg
 whites in a bowl 
over ice water, 
add sugar and 
beat until stiff 
peaks form

00:04:50.060 --> 00:05:00.440
<b>Cocoa
 Marshmallows</b>

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.940
Combine the two mixtures 
and beat at high speed 
 with a handheld mixer

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.270
Handheld mixers are incredible!

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.950
I bet you could manage with your 
hands alone, Ayase-senpai.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.440
<b>Pour into a mold and
 allow to set gradually</b>

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.440
<b>You can make a box out
of baking sheets, too.</b>

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.440
<b>Cut into small pieces with a
 knife coated in corn starch</b>

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.690
<b>Black Cocoa
Shortbread
Cookies</b>

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.500
They're so good!

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.330
And so cute!

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.810
Hanano-san, you're amazing!

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.170
The boys are going to be so happy!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:21.880
<b>Cocoa Marshmallows</b>

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:13.210
I wonder what kind of chocolate 
Mashima-senpai likes.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:21.880
<b>Black 
Cocoa
 Shortbread 
Cookies</b>

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:21.880
<b>Chocolate
Waffles</b>

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.190
I can't even imagine.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.830
Do you know, Chihaya-chan?

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.790
Oh, Taichi?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.880
He got tons of chocolates 
every year as a kid, so...

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.220
<b>Fermented 
Squid Guts</b>

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.210
He'd probably be happier to 
get fermented squid guts!

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.390
Are you serious?!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.720
Everything we just did was a total waste, then!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.420
Oh... Sorry.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.750
There are lots of boys like that, though.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.860
Should we make some fermented squid guts?

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:37.630
What?!

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.580
Right here? Right now? 
Fermented squid guts?!

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.070
Cocoa and fermented squid guts?!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.150
Nah, no way!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.730
Obviously not! Even a nice 
guy like him would barf!

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.420
The ribbons are so cute.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:52.700
If we're all eating them together in the
club room, why not prepare it as a picnic?

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.450
Good idea! Let's have fun with it!

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.360
Lots of fun!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.690
I like that color!

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.870
<i>Even a nice guy like him...</i>

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.760
<i>Someone so nice,</i>

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.720
<i>so strong,</i>

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:09.440
<i>who tries so hard...</i>

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.170
This...

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.430
This is fun.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:24.480
Doing things together 
with everyone is fun...

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.930
So why?

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.020
Why...

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.740
does Taichi seem so stressed out?

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:34.890
So in pain?

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:38.400
S... Sm...

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:41.670
Smile...

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.140
I want you to smile!

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.190
Thanks for having us.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:56.620
Chihaya-chan, make sure you don't 
forget to bring them tomorrow.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.540
Okay.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:02.880
It's pretty late, but I'm glad 
we got everything done.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.310
Hanano-san, is that...

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.930
Couverture chocolate, the kind they say
has a 100 percent chance of success?!

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.170
Oh...

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:14.060
Th-This is, um...

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:17.680
Were you late because you were buying that?

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.920
Chocolates for real love?

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:24.120
You're giving him those 
instead of homemade ones?

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.550
W-Well, they say it has a 
100 percent chance of success...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>Chance of success?</i>

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.490
<i>I know I don't even have one.</i>

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.950
<i>I know it's zero... but still...</i>

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:47.140
No matter what you give him, 
even if it's not on Valentine's Day,

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:50.060
I think you can get your feelings 
across whenever you want.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:55.770
Karuta was so far removed from you,
but you've worked hard at it this entire year.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.410
Your feelings have already taken shape.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:06.420
<b><i>Bubaigawara Station</i></b>

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.930
I'm headed this way. Bye, Hanano-san.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.420
Bye.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:13.670
<i>Everyone's thinking about you
on various levels,</i>

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.630
<i>so President... President...</i>

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.750
<i>Please cheer up.</i>

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.600
Thanks... a lot.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.460
Take mine too, Senpai!

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.040
Mine, too!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.520
Please accept mine!

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.510
He gets that many during every break.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:29.550
Mashima's been down lately, 
but I'm having trouble sympathizing.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.400
<b>Badump Badump</b>

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.120
<i>I can't catch him alone...</i>

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.700
Senpai!

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.950
<b>Badump Badump</b>

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.940
<i>I can't catch him alone!</i>

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.470
Eat these!

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.830
<b>Badump Badump</b>

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.570
<i>I can't catch him alone!</i>

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.200
<i>Hot guys...</i>

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.460
<i>are never alone...</i>

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.750
Crap! There's the bell!

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.090
<i>I don't absolutely have 
to give him these today.</i>

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.560
<i>I'll see him after school in the club room,</i>

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.590
<i>and I have no chance, anyway.</i>

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.540
<i>And he already knows how I feel...</i>

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.590
Mashima-senpai!

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.060
Here!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.990
<b>Heavy</b>

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.200
Wha—

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.490
H-Huh?

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.490
<b>Fermented Squid Guts</b>

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.500
Huh?

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.800
I like you, Senpai!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.250
I really like you!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.690
I want you

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.960
to tell the person you like
how you feel, too!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.680
Please tell them!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.450
Hey! Get to your classroom!

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.120
<i>Senpai... My dear Senpai...</i>

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.610
<i>I love you.</i>

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.430
I want you to smile!

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.250
<i>I know</i>

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.560
<i>Ayase-senpai does, too.</i>

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:29.970
<i>I know it!</i>

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:35.400
<b>Competitive
Karuta Club
New members always welcome!</b>

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:36.990
<b>Karuta Club Chocolate Festival</b>

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.240
<b>Karuta Club Chocolate Festival</b>

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.850
Wh-Wh-What is all this?!

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.300
What's going on in our sacred club room?!

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:46.510
Oh, will you leave, then?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.160
No!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.990
In fact, I'm calling my brothers!

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:52.150
Kana-chan, Sumire-chan, and I made them yesterday.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:52.880
They're homemade?!

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:53.730
Awesome!

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.650
Hanano-san's amazingly good at it.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.990
She brought all kinds of really 
heavy tools for us to use.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:58.620
Yeah?

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:02.000
I couldn't even picture 
Hanano cooking rice!

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.760
She's the type that can only 
make sweets! Totally!

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.080
Yeah, that's right. So what?

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.040
<i>Smile.</i>

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.260
<i>Smile, Taichi.</i>

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.420
<i>Smile, everyone!</i>

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.780
So today we're taking a break from karuta.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.280
We have chocolate waffles,

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.160
cocoa marshmallows, and black 
cocoa shortbread cookies!

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.490
They were delicious♥ 
But you made too many♥ 
Dad

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:31.980
<i>Our tremendous failure of a 
Valentine's Day ended...</i>

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.550
Dad!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.300
Chihaya! Thanks so much for the chocolates!

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:38.630
I know it's early, but I bought 
you something in return!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.550
<b>It's the night of 
February 14th, 
but still!</b>

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:37.610
D... Da...

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:39.730
D-Da...

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.280
I got some for your friends, too!

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.040
<i>And now it's March.</i>

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:51.140
Oe-senpai, I've been thinking 
about some things.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.060
What do you think about lash extensions?

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.100
What do you mean?

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:56.930
You know, eyelash extensions.

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:59.280
They're transplanted directly 
into your eyelashes.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:11:59.950
Transplanted?!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.560
But if you only have three 
eyelashes to begin with,

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:10.830
<b>Her commitment to beauty is intense...</b>

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:04.650
it'd just give you three 
or four times as many...

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:08.830
I also have some eyelash growth serum.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.440
I'll bring it next time.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.340
I need to ask you two something.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:17.560
<i>Spring.</i>

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:21.230
<i>The season when everything 
moves up one stage.</i>

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.220
Shizuoka Prefecture

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.220
Fujisaki High School
 Graduation Ceremony

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.000
Makoto-senpai!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:28.220
<b>Beautiful Boobs 
Collection</b>

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.220
Eromu-senpai, let me take a picture!

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:25.580
Masata-senpai!

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:25.680
Kanata-senpai!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.350
Mitsuki-senpai!

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:27.610
Pose for us!

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:28.220
Come visit the karuta club again!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.970
Senpai, look over here!

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:30.970
Look this way, please!

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.680
Emuro-senpai, don't do 
that with your hands!

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:32.930
Cheers, you're in the way!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.990
E-Everyone, don't stand here.

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:33.950
Your hair's curled too tight!

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:35.010
That's too forced!

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.310
You're blocking the way...

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.610
Makoto-senpai!

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.380
People!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:41.070
Say...

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:45.740
I thought the karuta club we created 
was more beautiful than this.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.730
What are you going to do, Rion?

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:52.370
Huh?

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:56.610
I'm going to college in Tokyo, 
and I'll be living on my own.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:57.670
Oh...

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:01.300
I mean, like, which karuta 
tournaments will you be in?

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.480
West or east?

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:04.190
Oh, excuse me. I got a message.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:07.190
Both are pretty easy to get 
to from Shizuoka, right?

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.770
So it doesn't matter which ones you go with...

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:12.390
But if possible, I hope you pick Tokyo.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.060
Then it'll be easy for us to see—

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.150
<b>Ayase-san?</b>

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:17.130
That's true... For starters, I'll go 
to the eastern tournament in April.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:20.150
Y-Yeah? Well, why not, right?

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:20.150
<b>I wonder where this is...</b>

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.650
Tokyo

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.650
Homei High School
Graduation Ceremony

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.720
You're so composed, Mr. Tsuboguchi...

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:28.160
<b>Year 3
 homeroom 
teacher</b>

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:28.150
Well, if I were a class teacher for third-years,
I might cry, too.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:32.700
Most of the kids in my karuta 
club were second-years,

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:38.290
<b>Homei High School Karuta Club</b>

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.720
so I guess next year is when I'll cry.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:38.280
That's true. All of the current 
generation graduates next year.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:43.920
Since the school added 
more courses aimed at
 boys, there are currently 
only eight first-year girls!
 It's projected there'll be 
ten next year and 250 boys...

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:42.810
Soon enough, there won't be a single 
girl left in the karuta club.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.300
<b>New Message 
Chihaya-chan</b>

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.220
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.260
Hokuo Academy
 Graduation Ceremony

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.370
Whew, thank goodness!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:54.730
Congratulations on Graduating

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:52.010
I won't be flicked in the 
forehead by Sudo-san anymore!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.470
That's honestly what's 
on my mind right now.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:58.480
Hokuo Academy Karuta Club Farewell Party

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.900
If I'm being even more honest,

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.340
I don't know if I'll keep 
playing karuta in college.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.490
Being in a karuta club 
at an all-boys school,

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:04.730
I've constantly been asked, 
"Why the karuta club?"

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.530
I get that!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:09.120
I've been playing since seventh grade, 
and I'm tired of explaining myself.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.990
I feel like I've done all I could, anyway.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:14.360
I guess you could say I've seen my limits.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.160
But...

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:23.180
Hokuo's capable of so much more!

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.980
It always has been!

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.530
And that...

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.170
makes me feel really frustrated.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:33.680
With the third-years gone, Shiroyama 
is the only Class A player left.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.720
Retro, as the new president,
you might be feeling a lot of pressure...

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.940
But your passion and pride

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:47.240
are unmatched in all of Tokyo, all of Japan. 
Everyone here knows that.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.190
So knock 'em dead!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.290
S-Someone, get some water!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.290
Wait, not a drink! He might need an IV!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.660
Retro won't stop crying! He's gonna dry up!

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.540
Incoming Message  Ayase Chihaya

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.790
<b>Tokyo 
Mizusawa 
High School</b>

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.170
I've just handed out

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.920
the results of this school year's 
final term exams.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.430
In April, you'll start studying 
for college entrance exams.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.430
Year: 2  Class: 1  Number: 10  Name: Komano Tsutomu 
Class Rank | Science Curriculum Rank

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:14.300
But don't jump the gun just yet.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:18.930
Only when study becomes a habit
can you call yourself an "exam student."

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:24.140
You study, ask questions,
gain an understanding, and practice.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.820
Has this become habitual for you?

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:29.950
Have you taken an interest in society?

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.960
College entrance exams test 
not only textbook knowledge,

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:35.950
but everything you've 
learned in your lives.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.570
Everything in my life?!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.060
Yikes...

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:44.530
Th-The Empress said that as 
Class 1's homeroom teacher!

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:45.730
You think so?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.420
<b>The advanced placement class...</b>

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:47.420
She wouldn't say that to Class 9!

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:52.920
Kind of makes you think it'll be impossible 
to balance studying and club stuff, huh?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.470
<b><i>Bubaigawara Station</i></b>

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.230
Let's think about that 
when we're third-years!

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:59.760
You're not even listening, are you?

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:03.070
For starters, on the first Saturday in April,
 we'll go see the cherry blossoms!

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.180
Huh? Cherry blossoms?

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.750
I'm gonna visit the bookstore 
before going home!

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:07.830
Er, then I'll come with—

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:10.360
Don't! I'm buying a book
I can't tell anyone about!

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:13.450
Eyelashes?

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.320
Hiroshi-san?

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.950
Huh? Hiroshi-san?

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.190
Wait, wait, wait!

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:22.320
This isn't right, Hiroshi-san!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:26.960
<b>Took 
off his 
uniform 
necktie</b>

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:25.980
What's not? Kids come to izakaya 
all the time nowadays.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.390
Keep me company.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:28.590
Here! Cheers!

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.590
<b>*Ordered 5 glasses to start</b>

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:31.600
Hurry up and turn twenty, would you?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.340
<b>*Drinks them all to start</b>

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:36.800
<b>More!</b>

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:41.070
Whew... I've been wanting to 
ask this for a long time.

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:44.440
How'd your match with Wataya-kun go?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.620
<i>Everything you've learned in your lives...</i>

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.040
It was like being an exam student.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.300
What does that mean?

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:11.800
He studies, asks questions,
gains an understanding, and practices.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:14.520
This has become habitual for him.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:19.730
It was like he'd spent his 
entire life preparing

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:23.390
in order to become the Master...

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:27.670
And like he was enjoying it.

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:30.440
He's gonna be the Master!

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.100
Here you go.

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.210
You're really something, Eyelashes.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.100
You think the two of you 
are that different,

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.850
but you can still feel frustrated.

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:51.110
Sorry to make you keep me company.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:52.130
It's okay.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.620
I should've tried to talk to you sooner.

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:55.700
No, it's not a problem.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:58.720
Goodnight.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.980
Chihaya-chan asked me.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:08.650
She asked me to get you to talk.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:16.490
I bet she just wanted to 
know about Arata, right?

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:20.210
That's what you think? You sure are dumb.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.480
Goodnight.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.220
You're so lucky!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:29.330
March 14th 
Class Duty 
Yuino  Yamai

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.340
You got a gift in return for 
Valentine's Day? A wallet?

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:32.450
Wow, must be nice to have a boyfriend.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:35.180
You still haven't given up 
on Mashima-senpai, Sumire?

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:37.020
It's never gonna happen.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.580
Plenty of fish in the sea.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.880
I mean, a guy with his looks named 
"Taichi"? It just feels wrong.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:42.350
Yeah, it means "the fattest"!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:44.350
What's wrong with being fat?!

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.600
S-S-Senpai!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.190
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:52.960
Nah, I've wondered why I got stuck with 
this name ever since I was a kid.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.620
Taichi's a great name! It's totally fine!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.610
<b>I figured a mom like her would've come up with a flashier name</b>

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:56.180
Here.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:19:00.490
It's not much, but it's in return 
for the fermented squid guts.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:02.530
Thanks.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:04.490
<i>I really like you!</i>

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:06.990
<i>I want you</i>

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:09.780
<i>to tell the person you like
how you feel, too!</i>

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.620
I think... I'm gonna go tell her.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.290
What?! Tell her what?!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.450
What... you...

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:17.750
Right now?!

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:18.860
Well, not this very—

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:19.750
Don't do it!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:20.420
Huh?

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:21.880
J-Just wait two more weeks!

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:22.130
Huh?

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:24.060
I-I need to go see Oe-senpai!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.040
I promised to give her 
eyelash growth serum!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.140
<b>You can't tell her right now!</b>

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.080
Huh?!

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.040
Just wait two weeks, please!

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:27.430
<b>Don't! Don't you dare!</b>

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.070
Eyelash growth?

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:31.900
Sorry I'm late!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.440
You certainly are late, Hanano-san!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.970
We need to be in the club room getting 
ready every day of spring break!

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:37.760
Chihaya-chan's been working hard, too.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.700
<b>As fast as an old-school flip phone allows</b>

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.680
She's gotten really fast 
at typing messages!

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:44.020
Mr. Mochida said we can borrow cards from 
the High School Cultural Federation if we ask.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.980
I sent messages out to everyone.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:49.280
I asked Porky's sister to 
make T-shirts for us, too.

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:52.470
Kana-chan, how much should we make
 the entry fee to even out the budget?

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:55.030
Just a second. I'm almost 
done working it out.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:58.310
Oe-senpai, here.

00:19:58.310 --> 00:19:58.910
Huh?

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.690
The eyelash growth serum.

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:01.650
Huh?!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:05.170
It works okay-ish, but I don't need it anymore.

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:10.390
I think... I'm gonna go tell her.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.080
<i>I wanted to be pretty.</i>

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:20.410
<i>I wanted to be pretty...</i>

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.950
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.150
Okay! I'm ready to work, too!

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:28.130
Make a roster!

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:29.320
Give me the data!

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.800
Who made this design for the T-shirts?!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:36.800
My sister's already started making them!

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.330
<i>That's not what it means to like someone.</i>

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:39.080
This design's fine, right?

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.100
What?!

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.720
<i>It's greedy, tenacious, and...</i>

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:45.540
<i>I want to make Taichi happy!</i>

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.520
So where are we going to 
look at cherry blossoms?

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:50.720
Where should we reserve a spot?

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:52.810
Put this T-shirt on, Taichi!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.860
Huh? What the heck is—

00:20:56.200 --> 00:21:00.920
<i>Because I didn't fulfill my goal on Valentine's
 Day, my desire grew even more intense.</i>

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:05.490
<b><i>Fuchu City Katamachi Cultural Center</i></b>

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.840
Wait, this is...

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:05.480
Taichi, today's your birthday, right?

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.480
Happy birthday!

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:12.830
<i>On April 2nd,</i>

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:17.120
<i>at the Fuchu City Katamachi Cultural 
Center in Bubaigawara...</i>

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.750
<b>The Taichi Cup</b>

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:23.120
<i>the volunteer-operated Taichi Cup
is about to begin.</i>

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:30.010
<b>The Taichi Cup 
Star</b>

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.810
<i>What... the... heck?!</i>
